      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63107",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/5a/5a1f383852538945b0a83fc8ac7e87654a05407079d50604646820de5988c965.png)\n\nThe dot plot above gives the number of pairs of shoes bought by a group of customers in a small shoe store. Each dot represents a single customer.\n\nThe frequency table below represents the same information. What number is missing from the table?\n\n| Number of Pairs of Shoes | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ | $4$ |\n| $2$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $2$ |\n| $4$ | $0$ |"
